{"assets":["/statement-assets/af572790d886b5de9e6a69678560f5b9ffb802b8d91d49716b2f7199c5afce2c.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"735","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Urbanization"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Local authorities have heard a lot about combinatorial abilities of Ostap Bender so they decided to ask his help in the question of urbanization. There are "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" people who plan to move to the cities. The wealth of the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" of them is equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":". Authorities plan to build two cities, first for "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n1"},{"kind":"text","text":" people and second for "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n2"},{"kind":"text","text":" people. Of course, each of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" candidates can settle in only one of the cities. Thus, first some subset of candidates of size "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n1"},{"kind":"text","text":" settle in the first city and then some subset of size "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n2"},{"kind":"text","text":" is chosen among the remaining candidates and the move to the second city. All other candidates receive an official refuse and go back home."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To make the statistic of local region look better in the eyes of their bosses, local authorities decided to pick subsets of candidates in such a way that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"the sum of arithmetic mean"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of wealth of people in each of the cities is as large as possible. Arithmetic mean of wealth in one city is the sum of wealth "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" among all its residents divided by the number of them ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n1"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n2"},{"kind":"text","text":" depending on the city). The division should be done in real numbers without any rounding."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Please, help authorities find the optimal way to pick residents for two cities."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains three integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n1"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n2"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n, n1, n2 ≤ 100 000"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n1 + n2 ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of candidates who want to move to the cities, the planned number of residents of the first city and the planned number of residents of the second city."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1, a2, ..., an"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ ai ≤ 100 000"},{"kind":"text","text":"), the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th of them is equal to the wealth of the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th candidate."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print one real value — the maximum possible sum of arithmetic means of wealth of cities' residents. You answer will be considered correct if its absolute or relative error does not exceed "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"10 - 6"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Namely: let's assume that your answer is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":", and the answer of the jury is "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"b"},{"kind":"text","text":". The checker program will consider your answer correct, if "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/af572790d886b5de9e6a69678560f5b9ffb802b8d91d49716b2f7199c5afce2c.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2 1 1\n1 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"6.00000000\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4 2 1\n1 4 2 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"6.50000000\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample, one of the optimal solutions is to move candidate "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to the first city and candidate "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" to the second."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second sample, the optimal solution is to pick candidates "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":" for the first city, and candidate "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" for the second one. Thus we obtain "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(a3 + a4) / 2 + a2 = (3 + 2) / 2 + 4 = 6.5"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"735B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/735/problem/B"}